#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151846 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152097 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d2f207a-8e99-5520-ab9f-266c8f54465b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements Belonging to a Residue Class"}] :question/id #uuid "41276052-e364-593e-9557-5d645f169a74" :question/math-academy-id "e-14600" :question/problem "Which of the following integers belong to the residue class $[5]_{8}?$\n\n- $-3$\n\n- $13$\n\n- $3$" :question/worked-solution "The residue class $[5]_{8}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $5$ modulo $8.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[5]_{8} & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡5\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x=5+8k,\\,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={5+8k\\,|\\,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={…,\\,5-2\\cdot 8,\\,5-8,\\,5,\\,5+8,\\,5+2\\cdot 8,\\,…} \\\\  & ={…,-11,-3,5,13,21,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $-3$ and $13$ belong to $[5]_{8},$ while $3$ does not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151847 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152098 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c1fe7ea-d91e-5440-b756-37a460a18f19" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Residue Classes Containing a Given Element"}] :question/id #uuid "33da67df-113b-58e2-ad3e-a45d1568d75d" :question/math-academy-id "e-14601" :question/problem "Which of the following residue classes modulo $3$ contain the integer $7?$\n\n- $[4]_3$\n\n- $[-1]_3$\n\n- $[1]_3$" :question/worked-solution "We have $7 \\in [a]_{3}$ if \n\n$$\n7 \\equiv a \\quad (\\text{mod}\\:3).\n$$\n\nLet's now consider each of the given equivalence classes.\n\n- $7 \\in [4]_3$ because $7 \\equiv 4 \\: (\\text{mod}\\:3)$ $\\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n\n- $7 \\not\\in [-1]_3$ because $7 \\not\\equiv -1 \\: (\\text{mod}\\:3)$ $\\quad \\color{red}\\times$\n\n- $7 \\in [1]_3$ because $7 \\equiv 1 \\: (\\text{mod}\\:3)$ $\\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151848 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152099 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6097ae19-85d5-5ca9-892d-889e843b3def" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalent Residue Classes"}] :question/id #uuid "edf5a7d6-354d-534b-a8d3-5b29f2357a70" :question/math-academy-id "e-14602" :question/problem "If $[a]_n$ denotes the residue class containing all integers congruent to $a$ modulo $n,$ then which of the following residue classes is equal to $[13]_3?$\n\n- $[0]_3$\n\n- $[1]_3$\n\n- $[2]_3$" :question/worked-solution "We have $[a]_{3} = [b]_{3}$ if \n\n$$\na \\equiv b \\quad (\\text{mod}\\:3).\n$$\n\nThe residue class $[13]_{3}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $13$ modulo $3.$ \n\nWe can find an alternative representation for this residue class as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[13]_{3} & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡13\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡4\\cdot 3+1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡4\\cdot 0+1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)} \\\\  & =[1]_{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151850 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152100 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d1a842b5-7256-59cd-b33f-d590bc315d84" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements"}] :question/id #uuid "e8470a32-e938-5ae5-a732-688a6d62cefd" :question/math-academy-id "e-14604" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- There are $4$ distinct residue classes modulo $8$\n\n- $[5]_{3} \\cap [9]_{3} = \\emptyset$\n\n- $\\mathbb{Z} = [4]_{3} \\cup [5]_{3} \\cup [9]_{3}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the residue classes modulo $n$ have the following properties:\n\n- There are exactly $n$ distinct residue classes modulo $n$\n\n- Two distinct residue classes have an empty intersection: $[a]_n \\cap [b]_n = \\emptyset$ if $a \\not\\equiv b \\: (\\text{mod}\\:n)$\n\n- Residue classes modulo $n$ form a partition of the set of all integers: \n\n$$\n\\mathbb{Z} = [0]_n \\cup [1]_n \\cup \\cdots \\cup [n-1]_n\n$$\n\n- The integers modulo $n$ is defined as the set containing all distinct residue classes modulo $n$: \n\n$$\n\\mathbb{Z}_n = \\big\\{[0]_n,\\, [1]_n,\\, \\ldots,\\,  [n-1]_n\\big\\}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now consider each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. There are exactly $8$ distinct residue classes modulo $8.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, since $5 \\not\\equiv 9 \\: (\\text{mod }3),$ we have that $[5]_3\\cap [9]_3= \\emptyset.$\n\n- Statement III is true. First, notice the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[4]_{3} & =[1+3\\cdot 1]_{3}=[1]_{3} \\\\ [5]_{3} & =[2+3\\cdot 1]_{3}=[2]_{3} \\\\ [9]_{3} & =[0+3\\cdot 3]_{3}=[0]_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[4]_{3}\\cup [5]_{3}\\cup [9]_{3} & =[1]_{3}\\cup [2]_{3}\\cup [0]_{3} \\\\  & =[0]_{3}\\cup [1]_{3}\\cup [2]_{3} \\\\  & =Z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412964 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152097 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d2f207a-8e99-5520-ab9f-266c8f54465b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements Belonging to a Residue Class"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ae50f18-3a44-5059-859d-62a308e0626c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412825} {:answer/id #uuid "536a2ad9-31ea-58bb-ad50-9a311d120bc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412841} {:answer/id #uuid "6e813eca-88bc-51a0-a774-be6fb12da67f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412854} {:answer/id #uuid "a3be6687-8c01-58a1-8b6f-55c990a13f73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412883} {:answer/id #uuid "ddf198f1-51ce-5197-901f-4a57ec6ca534" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412916}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3be6687-8c01-58a1-8b6f-55c990a13f73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412883} :answer-field/id #uuid "86eeeda2-7dc4-5dc4-b9bd-b1e07b0c7e13" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412941}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "44e36839-2675-57c4-abf9-91a0b0717003" :question/math-academy-id "q-214450" :question/problem "Which of the following integers belong to the residue class $[4]_{7}?$\n\n- $-3$\n- $6$\n- $18$" :question/worked-solution "The residue class $[4]_{7}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $4$ modulo $7.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[4]_{7} & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡4\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x=4+7k,\\,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={4+7k\\,|\\,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={…,\\,4-2\\cdot 7,\\,4-7,\\,4,\\,4+7,\\,4+2\\cdot 7,\\,…} \\\\  & ={…,-10,-3,4,11,18,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $-3$ and $18$ belong to $[4]_{7},$ while $6$ does not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412960 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152099 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6097ae19-85d5-5ca9-892d-889e843b3def" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalent Residue Classes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c2050fc-dd72-59da-bd00-d4fb4787ba45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[5]_{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412837} {:answer/id #uuid "a7d1238b-22f5-51bf-ad99-330fde0e0432" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[1]_{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412884} {:answer/id #uuid "c27ce301-a593-5534-a045-c8e23fc79bb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[0]_{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412897} {:answer/id #uuid "c5856a96-f7b4-5c0c-8c44-8b6c81d37607" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[4]_{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412901} {:answer/id #uuid "e468ea16-7d58-5381-9c3e-97010cf5f55b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[2]_{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412919}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5856a96-f7b4-5c0c-8c44-8b6c81d37607" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[4]_{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412901} :answer-field/id #uuid "81087f72-4918-5614-9cfb-be935bd74663" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412940}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0c2846ce-57fa-59ad-9fe2-ab1c6ed9c653" :question/math-academy-id "q-214477" :question/problem "If $[a]_{n}$ denotes the residue class containing all integers congruent to $a$ modulo $n,$ then $[-26]_{6}=$" :question/worked-solution "We have $[a]_{6}=[b]_{6}$ if \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6).\n$$\n\nThe residue class $[-26]_{6}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $-26$ modulo $6.$ \n\nWe can find an alternative representation for this residue class as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[-26]_{6} & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡-26\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡(-5)\\cdot 6+4\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡(-5)\\cdot 0+4\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡4\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)} \\\\  & =[4]_{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412963 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152100 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d1a842b5-7256-59cd-b33f-d590bc315d84" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "857b9969-8eba-5781-8889-8c40601d739d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[0]_{12}\\cup [1]_{12}\\cup ⋯\\cup [11]_{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412871} {:answer/id #uuid "fbb651a7-816e-5e1e-b969-b531e801dac3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[0]_{12}\\,,[1]_{12},…\\,,[11]_{12}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412927}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fbb651a7-816e-5e1e-b969-b531e801dac3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[0]_{12}\\,,[1]_{12},…\\,,[11]_{12}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412927} :answer-field/id #uuid "27247094-17db-5e37-bcae-0cf5549e29af" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412933} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ce65867-512d-5702-9764-2b6aa07f82be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[0]_{12}\\cup [1]_{12}\\cup ⋯\\cup [11]_{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412853} {:answer/id #uuid "83f61a34-c667-57ee-8f9e-eebd8d8b20ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[0]_{12}\\cap [1]_{12}\\cap ⋯\\cap [11]_{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412869}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ce65867-512d-5702-9764-2b6aa07f82be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[0]_{12}\\cup [1]_{12}\\cup ⋯\\cup [11]_{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412853} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1d15121-09a7-5bb5-9596-3cceaf06e5cd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412945} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c082879-e35e-529b-bf83-498ccc230eb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[3]_{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412826} {:answer/id #uuid "59a755d6-dd21-56a7-a444-c6a85453eee1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412846} {:answer/id #uuid "608ab3d0-e141-5dba-86be-118421761875" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412850}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59a755d6-dd21-56a7-a444-c6a85453eee1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412846} :answer-field/id #uuid "f018e54d-142b-5443-b618-b3c381ce86eb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412953}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "32f1fbfd-ebfc-5a37-bf9e-b69da2b29724" :question/math-academy-id "q-214479" :question/problem "Select the correct options in the statements below regarding residue classes modulo $12:$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the residue classes modulo $n$ have the following properties:\n\n- There are exactly $n$ distinct residue classes modulo $n$\n\n- Two distinct residue classes have an empty intersection: $[a]_{n}\\cap [b]_{n}=∅$ if $a≢b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)$\n\n- Residue classes modulo $n$ form a partition of the set of all integers: \n\n$$\nZ=[0]_{n}\\cup [1]_{n}\\cup ⋯\\cup [n-1]_{n}\n$$\n\n- The integers modulo $n$ is defined as the set containing all distinct residue classes modulo $n$: \n\n$$\n{Z}_{n}={[0]_{n},\\,[1]_{n},\\,…,\\,[n-1]_{n}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following properties:\n\n- $[0]_{12}\\cap [6]_{12}=∅.$\n\n- $Z=[0]_{12}\\cup [1]_{12}\\cup ⋯\\cup [11]_{12}.$\n\n- ${Z}_{12}={[0]_{12},[1]_{12},⋯,[11]_{12}}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412968 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152100 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d1a842b5-7256-59cd-b33f-d590bc315d84" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a59bc11-205d-5538-909d-cbd2ef20b03f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412835} {:answer/id #uuid "524616ef-b4aa-5821-952e-2d370c8b92fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412839} {:answer/id #uuid "7031c594-1614-52f5-bbca-a4d2867b00e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412857} {:answer/id #uuid "73af8c90-ce2b-5afd-ada7-58ab041cddc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412858} {:answer/id #uuid "81e51a0c-ed4c-5398-bdc0-1626c1168148" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412866} {:answer/id #uuid "97e24b16-8860-55e1-b3db-ef84b5cc81d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412880}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7031c594-1614-52f5-bbca-a4d2867b00e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412857} :answer-field/id #uuid "37ae3642-035a-599a-a72e-0d5e712e7054" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412935} {:answer-field/choices [{:ans