d22994846" :question/math-academy-id "q-214481" :question/problem "Select the correct options in the statements below regarding residue classes modulo $11:$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the residue classes modulo $n$ have the following properties:\n\n- There are exactly $n$ distinct residue classes modulo $n$\n\n- Two distinct residue classes have an empty intersection: $[a]_{n}\\cap [b]_{n}=∅$ if $a≢b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)$\n\n- Residue classes modulo $n$ form a partition of the set of all integers: \n\n$$\nZ=[0]_{n}\\cup [1]_{n}\\cup ⋯\\cup [n-1]_{n}\n$$\n\n- The integers modulo $n$ is defined as the set containing all distinct residue classes modulo $n$: \n\n$$\n{Z}_{n}={[0]_{n},\\,[1]_{n},\\,…,\\,[n-1]_{n}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following properties:\n\n- There are $11$ distinct residue classes modulo $11.$\n\n- $[5]_{11}\\cap [10]_{11}=∅.$\n\n- ${Z}_{11}={[0]_{11},\\,[1]_{11},\\,…,\\,[10]_{11}}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412973 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152100 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d1a842b5-7256-59cd-b33f-d590bc315d84" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81d3b236-8c95-5efb-8005-fa1b11cdc234" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412865} {:answer/id #uuid "95432755-0f48-5475-a6a1-bfa70aebc37e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412878} {:answer/id #uuid "fbaaee8e-3968-5cd4-a632-19f885bc7666" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412926}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81d3b236-8c95-5efb-8005-fa1b11cdc234" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412865} :answer-field/id #uuid "16083492-fd9b-5d22-9677-01e13fa