sidue class modulo $223$ containing the element $i\\in Z.$ Select the correct options in the statements below." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the residue classes modulo $n$ have the following properties:\n\n- There are exactly $n$ distinct residue classes modulo $n$\n\n- Two distinct residue classes have an empty intersection: $[a]_{n}\\cap [b]_{n}=∅$ if $a≢b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)$\n\n- Residue classes modulo $n$ form a partition of the set of all integers: \n\n$$\nZ=[0]_{n}\\cup [1]_{n}\\cup ⋯\\cup [n-1]_{n}\n$$\n\n- The integers modulo $n$ is defined as the set containing all distinct residue classes modulo $n$: \n\n$$\n{Z}_{n}={[0]_{n},\\,[1]_{n},\\,…,\\,[n-1]_{n}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following properties:\n\n- ${⋃}_{i=0}^{222}\\,[\\,i\\,]_{223}=Z$\n\n- $[\\,21\\,]_{223}\\cap [\\,162\\,]_{223}=∅$\n\n- ${Z}_{223}={[\\,i\\,]_{223}\\,∣\\,0\\le i<223}$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412972 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152097 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d2f207a-8e99-5520-ab9f-266c8f54465b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements Belonging to a Residue Class"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d6e5a94-ee4d-53e1-8683-a2c6015c7c95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412827} {:answer/id #uuid "5479ed01-e1d6-5e5a-b01f-9abefb2c6a10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412842} {:answer/id #uuid "c2eeae29-6589-5372-9208-8579d86384ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412898} {:answer/id #uuid "c8b963dd-bb5a-5a02-9158-70da5aa07a71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412903} {:answer/id #uuid "fc4562a3-8e24-54b7-820d-6e3b72017105" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412928}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2eeae29-6589-5372-9208-8579d86384ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412898} :answer-field/id #uuid "99eba53e-9c7a-538e-95be-f63aec7390ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412943}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "abd84654-ac2d-58a6-9574-529f2b4aa6f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-78597" :question/problem "Which of the following integers belong to the residue class $[-7]_{11}?$\n\n- $15$\n- $-4$\n- $7$" :question/worked-solution "The residue class $[-7]_{11}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $-7$ modulo $11.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[-7]_{11} & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡-7\\,(\\text{mod}\\,11)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x=-7+11k,\\,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={-7+11k\\,|\\,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={…,\\,-7-2\\cdot 11,\\,-7-11,\\,-7,\\,-7+11,\\,-7+2\\cdot 11,\\,…} \\\\  & ={…,-29,-18,-7,4,15,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $15$ belongs to $[-7]_{11},$ while $-4$ and $7$ do not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152792 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152097 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d2f207a-8e99-5520-ab9f-266c8f54465b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements Belonging to a Residue Class"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1033dd79-9600-51c4-a8ca-3a31c3dde48f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412816} {:answer/id #uuid "6ef83927-2628-5d68-bf65-a48c1fe20d5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412856} {:answer/id #uuid "8508cb49-93b9-537a-b130-be5b95ed2386" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412870} {:answer/id #uuid "88959a9d-340f-5ee1-b746-8a0de81e8b1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412873} {:answer/id #uuid "c35aa81f-3a6b-57fc-9666-5deb89ff8dcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412900}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8508cb49-93b9-537a-b130-be5b95ed2386" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412870} :answer-field/id #uuid "cce84edd-038c-58d1-9051-41a39c1a5bad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412948}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ba3bb1ff-f2f2-5531-a68f-b27801ed7066" :question/math-academy-id "q-78598" :question/problem "Which of the following integers belong to the residue class $[6]_{9}?$\n\n- $-12$\n- $3$\n- $24$" :question/worked-solution "The residue class $[6]_{9}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $6$ modulo $9.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[6]_{9} & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡6\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x=6+9k,\\,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={6+9k\\,|\\,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={…,\\,6-2\\cdot 9,\\,6-9,\\,6,\\,6+9,\\,6+2\\cdot 9,\\,…} \\\\  & ={…,-12,-3,6,15,24,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $-12$ and $24$ belong to $[6]_{9},$ while $3$ does not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412971 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152097 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d2f207a-8e99-5520-ab9f-266c8f54465b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements Belonging to a Residue Class"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14030e88-6395-56f9-82ae-0053228a0a90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412817} {:answer/id #uuid "8ed69294-b796-5762-a670-e84ffa5fce8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412874} {:answer/id #uuid "a892cb8e-e16a-5a18-b277-91ca8afd57cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412885} {:answer/id #uuid "d22c7286-cdcb-5191-9d60-a9974ca672d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412909} {:answer/id #uuid "d73fae85-da65-51ae-ad7a-ae836d3b1e11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412914}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d22c7286-cdcb-5191-9d60-a9974ca672d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412909} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4475c97-7935-5890-8ef0-c7a0d0f183f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412957}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a55de8de-5dbf-5007-a3cb-517652d485f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-78599" :question/problem "Which of the following integers belong to the residue class $[9]_{13}?$\n\n- $4$\n- $-17$\n- $35$" :question/worked-solution "The residue class $[9]_{13}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $9$ modulo $13.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[9]_{13} & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡9\\,(\\text{mod}\\,13)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x=9+13k,\\,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={9+13k\\,|\\,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={…,\\,9-2\\cdot 13,\\,9-13,\\,9,\\,9+13,\\,9+2\\cdot 13,\\,…} \\\\  & ={…,-17,-4,9,22,35,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $-17$ and $35$ belong to $[9]_{13},$ while $4$ does not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412965 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152098 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c1fe7ea-d91e-5440-b756-37a460a18f19" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Residue Classes Containing a Given Element"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a9a1c5c-d379-566e-88ec-4f742d23a956" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412830} {:answer/id #uuid "3cdd9f0e-932d-558a-9378-6f478cae4f32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412831} {:answer/id #uuid "d3abf09a-f4e8-5b21-bd9a-3231221ada27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412910} {:answer/id #uuid "d5516742-1e80-5031-a6c5-e5f0e763ef73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412913} {:answer/id #uuid "ef8754b8-9881-5ed1-bb9f-dc739076a719" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412923}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d5516742-1e80-5031-a6c5-e5f0e763ef73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412913} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c42e18f-3211-5db3-867f-3fb18fe023c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412942}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "476816fb-a049-55c8-86b3-04683cf8a95e" :question/math-academy-id "q-78604" :question/problem "Which of the following residue classes modulo $6$ contain the integer $7?$\n\n- $[-5]_{6}$\n- $[3]_{6}$\n- $[1]_{6}$" :question/worked-solution "We have $7\\in [a]_{6}$ if \n\n$$\n7≡a\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6).\n$$\n\nLet's now consider each of the given equivalence classes.\n\n- $7\\in [-5]_{6}$ because $7≡-5\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)$ $\\,✓$\n\n- $7\\notin [3]_{6}$ because $7≢3\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- $7\\in [1]_{6}$ because $7≡1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)$ $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412961 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152100 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d1a842b5-7256-59cd-b33f-d590bc315d84" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a74b48c-8a09-5420-9014-3039dfa306ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412824} {:answer/id #uuid "5b3caf48-3d6b-58e9-8443-a76f248d4f34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412848} {:answer/id #uuid "5f50b178-baf5-50bc-b791-e2b9c9ce601d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412849} {:answer/id #uuid "7ba5e226-5ed0-5aa6-8f25-569b9054ddde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412862} {:answer/id #uuid "c31a23b5-9755-5c42-94ff-b6938dbd6b75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412899}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c31a23b5-9755-5c42-94ff-b6938dbd6b75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412899} :answer-field/id #uuid "2372040f-636b-51db-a88a-0a20d411e932" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412932}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0f9012f2-83ba-5f6f-b553-2ea47d5d4f81" :question/math-academy-id "q-78640" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- There are $3$ distinct residue classes modulo $6$\n- $[5]_{3}\\cap [1]_{3}\\ne ∅$\n- $Z=[3]_{2}\\cup [6]_{2}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the residue classes modulo $n$ have the following properties:\n\n- There are exactly $n$ distinct residue classes modulo $n$\n\n- Two distinct residue classes have an empty intersection: $[a]_{n}\\cap [b]_{n}=∅$ if $a≢b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)$\n\n- Residue classes modulo $n$ form a partition of the set of all integers: \n\n$$\nZ=[0]_{n}\\cup [1]_{n}\\cup ⋯\\cup [n-1]_{n}\n$$\n\n- The integers modulo $n$ is defined as the set containing all distinct residue classes modulo $n$: \n\n$$\n{Z}_{n}={[0]_{n},\\,[1]_{n},\\,…,\\,[n-1]_{n}}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now consider each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. There are exactly $6$ distinct residue classes modulo $6.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $5≢1\\,(\\text{mod }3),$ we have that $[5]_{3}\\cap [1]_{3}=∅.$\n\n- Statement III is true. First, notice the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[3]_{2} & =[1+2\\cdot 1]_{2}=[1]_{2} \\\\ [6]_{2} & =[0+2\\cdot 3]_{2}=[0]_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[3]_{2}\\cup [6]_{2} & =[1]_{2}\\cup [0]_{2} \\\\  & =[0]_{2}\\cup [1]_{2} \\\\  & =Z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412977 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152100 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d1a842b5-7256-59cd-b33f-d590bc315d84" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "406d20f8-1407-5435-8784-5f3e29ff681c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412834} {:answer/id #uuid "4a92891f-39e5-5cee-b46a-8784882f23fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412836} {:answer/id #uuid "52eadcaf-a11c-568b-907e-2ff81396dc49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412840} {:answer/id #uuid "7ecfdc45-6d9f-55e1-936c-36ea7836a224" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412864} {:answer/id #uuid "ccfb74cf-ee0e-514f-afc8-cbb35b8f9393" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412905}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ccfb74cf-ee0e-514f-afc8-cbb35b8f9393" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412905} :answer-field/id #uuid "0dd3a9af-e1c5-54e0-8441-f550817b9384" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412929}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f68491fc-7fbf-551d-bb56-21bac80c159f" :question/math-academy-id "q-78644" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- There are $11$ distinct residue classes modulo $11$\n- $[7]_{5}\\cap [2]_{5}\\ne ∅$\n- $Z=[0]_{4}\\cup [9]_{4}\\cup [2]_{4}\\cup [15]_{4}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the residue classes modulo $n$ have the following properties:\n\n- There are exactly $n$ distinct residue classes modulo $n$\n\n- Two distinct residue classes have an empty intersection: $[a]_{n}\\cap [b]_{n}=∅$ if $a≢b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)$\n\n- Residue classes modulo $n$ form a partition of the set of all integers: \n\n$$\nZ=[0]_{n}\\cup [1]_{n}\\cup ⋯\\cup [n-1]_{n}\n$$\n\n- The integers modulo $n$ is defined as the set containing all distinct residue classes modulo $n$: \n\n$$\n{Z}_{n}={[0]_{n},\\,[1]_{n},\\,…,\\,[n-1]_{n}}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now consider each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. There are $11$ distinct residue classes modulo $11.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, since $7≡2\\,(\\text{mod }5),$ we have that $[7]_{5}=[2]_{5}.$ Therefore, $[7]_{5}\\cap [2]_{5}\\ne ∅.$\n\n- Statement III is true. First, notice the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[9]_{4} & =[1+4\\cdot 2]_{4}=[1]_{4} \\\\ [15]_{4} & =[3+4\\cdot 3]_{4}=[3]_{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[0]_{4}\\cup [9]_{4}\\cup [2]_{4}\\cup [15]_{4} & =[0]_{4}\\cup [1]_{4}\\cup [2]_{4}\\cup [3]_{4} \\\\  & =Z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412976 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152097 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d2f207a-8e99-5520-ab9f-266c8f54465b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements Belonging to a Residue Class"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16580a0c-365e-59a9-9828-bb02a47e8573" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412819} {:answer/id #uuid "7e33db2a-1dbd-5414-9540-709392a7913f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412863} {:answer/id #uuid "abb17be0-afe8-5a6d-8ef7-96917a6efd85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412889} {:answer/id #uuid "b9bdbd57-ea56-5ecb-8fe2-07753e9011a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412893} {:answer/id #uuid "c638689c-94e7-5af8-b84c-75a738f6395e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412902}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16580a0c-365e-59a9-9828-bb02a47e8573" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412819} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2e9f81c-9578-565c-8322-3231a43ad273" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412956}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e91f8fe9-c6f2-558a-bf39-b0389019d5ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-86021" :question/problem "Which of the following integers belong to the residue class $[7]_{11}?$\n\n- $18$\n- $-4$\n- $15$" :question/worked-solution "The residue class $[7]_{11}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $7$ modulo $11.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[7]_{11} & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡7\\,(\\text{mod}\\,11)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x=7+11k,\\,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={7+11k\\,|\\,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={…,\\,7-2\\cdot 11,\\,7-11,\\,7,\\,7+11,\\,7+2\\cdot 11,…} \\\\  & ={…,-15,-4,7,18,29,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $-4$ and $18$ belong to $[7]_{11},$ while $15$ does not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412969 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152098 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c1fe7ea-d91e-5440-b756-37