} \\\\  & =[2]_{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412959 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152099 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6097ae19-85d5-5ca9-892d-889e843b3def" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalent Residue Classes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03d0960c-af61-5116-9326-54622ce4d65f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[3]_{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412809} {:answer/id #uuid "579fee27-e1b5-5dfd-851e-08154afab314" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[0]_{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412845} {:answer/id #uuid "77d4339d-48cc-5e13-9ad6-28908953770a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[2]_{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412861} {:answer/id #uuid "961ca45e-d10a-5051-97be-d9e6f717d64f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[5]_{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412879} {:answer/id #uuid "d0255b94-ede3-5ce4-bb10-56451be8a87e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[4]_{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412908}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03d0960c-af61-5116-9326-54622ce4d65f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[3]_{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412809} :answer-field/id #uuid "3107f40f-9ecd-5896-b96d-bd32cac730cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412934}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "06e706ec-ef55-5e4d-a1fb-e7ced3a44078" :question/math-academy-id "q-86034" :question/problem "If $[a]_{n}$ denotes the residue class containing all integers congruent to $a$ modulo $n,$ then $[-21]_{6}=$" :question/worked-solution "We have $[a]_{6}=[b]_{6}$ if \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6).\n$$\n\nThe residue class $[-21]_{6}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $-21$ modulo $6.$ \n\nWe can find an alternative representation for this residue class as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[-21]_{6} & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡-21\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡(-4)\\cdot 6+3\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡(-4)\\cdot 0+3\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡3\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)} \\\\  & =[3]_{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412962 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152099 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6097ae19-85d5-5ca9-892d-889e843b3def" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalent Residue Classes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0636d430-5e30-5d21-8647-9ba69f94907c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[0]_{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412811} {:answer/id #uuid "3ebbd4db-2968-5f79-8339-3f181b9aa536" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[4]_{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412832} {:answer/id #uuid "952759eb-0e3e-5800-ac84-bf79ec646ecf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[2]_{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412877} {:answer/id #uuid "cc197bf1-e9bb-5eeb-be5f-93b0c73c79b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[3]_{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412904} {:answer/id #uuid "e37f517a-1c00-5080-a17b-5cfdbbd2da1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[1]_{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "952759eb-0e3e-5800-ac84-bf79ec646ecf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[2]_{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412877} :answer-field/id #uuid "d321d18